,title,link,text,language,family
0,Alas language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alas_language,"Alas-Kluet, Alas, or Batak Alas is an Austronesian language of Sumatra. The three dialects, Alas, Kluet, and Singkil (Kade-Kade), may not constitute a single language; Alas may be closer to Karo, and the others closer to Dairi. By linguistic affiliation, Alas–Kluet belongs to the Batak subgroup.",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
1,Alas people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alas_people,"The Alas people are an indigenous Batak sub-ethnic group from Southeast Aceh Regency, Aceh, Sumatra, Indonesia. The Alas are found in the Gunung Leuser, ...",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
2,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh9pFS_rqvm3r2JtCD8AGOa-,"Many of the indigenous peoples of India are considered to belong to the Australasian language group, while Austronesian culture arose from later migrations.",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
3,Alas language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/alas_language,"Spoken exclusively by the Alas people, who number about 95,000 (as of 2023) and maintain a patrilineal clan-based society focused on wet-rice agriculture and forest products, the language underscores their cultural identity amid historical ties to Batak migrations and distinctions from adjacent Gayo and Acehnese groups. [1]",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
4,Austronesian Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/austronesian-music/,"Austronesian music nowadays refers to the ongoing evolution and fusion of various cultural influences from foreign and neighbouring cultures. These influences have over the centuries introduced new instruments, styles, and genres, blending age-old elements with newer traditions.",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
5,Alas Ethnic Minority Music of Aceh: Canang Situ — aural ...,https://www.auralarchipelago.com/auralarchipelago/canangsitu,"Nov 26, 2022 · Ritual gong music played by women is not a total anomaly in Aceh - the Alas’ ethnic minority neighbors, the Gayo to the north and the Kluet to the south, also have strong traditions of women playing gongs, also called canang, at weddings and other ritual occasions.",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
6,"Batak Alas-Kluet Language (BTZ) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/btz/,"Batak Alas-Kluet is a stable indigenous language of Indonesia. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
7,Batak Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/batak-music/,"Music of the Batak people, an Austronesian people native to Sumatra. Read more The Batak comprise multiple closely related ethnic groups, primarily the Karo, Pakpak, Simalungun, Toba, Angkola and Mandailing, all of whom speak the Batak languages of the Austronesian family.",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
8,Batak languages: Northern and Southern branches - Facebook,https://www.facebook.com/groups/austronesian.languages/posts/938573713732311/,"Dec 28, 2021 ... BONE IN BATAK LANGUAGES BRANCH • Proto-Austronesian ... Batak Alas-Kluet 70. Batak Angkola 71. Batak Dairi 72. Batak Karo 73 ...",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
9,Batak languages (Hata Batak - Instagram,https://www.instagram.com/p/C5qHrldvoww/,"Apr 12, 2024 ... They consists of 7 variants namely Pakpak (Dairi), Karo, Alas-Kluet, Simalungun, Toba, Angkola and Mandailing. The Batak scripts used by these ...",Batak Alas-Kluet,Austronesian
